    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single stored `memberId` field formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. Verified end-to-end: the audit log now emits `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, FY `27`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, Luhn CHK `1`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`, with matching getter/setter.\n- **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 renamed the column and widened to `VARCHAR(32)` (the id can reach 18 chars for `UNKNOWN` regions plus a collision suffix).\n- **`CustomerCodes.java` \u2192 `MemberIds.java`** (renamed) \u2014 `forOwner` now builds `region + FY + HASH8 + CHK`, where CHK is `CheckDigits.luhn` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Same SHA-256-over-(E.164 telephone + lastName) HASH8 as before. `localityOf` now derives region from the postcode (behaviour-preserving \u2014 the old parse read back the same value).\n- **`AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2192 `AssignMemberId.java`** (renamed) \u2014 collision handling (`-<n>` suffix) now applies to `memberId`.\n- **`CheckDigits.java`** \u2014 dropped the `customerCode`-based `forOwner`; kept the shared `luhn` utility (now used for the CHK segment).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings; `memberId` maps automatically as a stored field; `locality`/`timezone` point at `MemberIds`.\n- **`OwnerSegments.java`, `Digests.java`** \u2014 updated references to `MemberIds`.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 human line and JSON event now carry `memberId`; `primaryIdentifier` returns it.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 `assignCode` step wired to `AssignMemberId`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the three field schemas with a single documented `memberId`.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the `-<n>` collision suffix appends *after* the CHK, so a colliding id becomes e.g. `NSW27...1-2` (the CHK still validates only the base). That preserves the prior collision semantics; if you'd prefer the suffix folded into the Luhn or a different disambiguation scheme, let me know.",
